# gnome.folder — desktop-file IDs grouped into the "w1ld0s" app-grid folder.
# Consumed by modules/07-gnome-shell.sh
# (org.gnome.desktop.app-folders.folder:/…/folders/w1ld0s/ apps).
#
# One ID per line, WITH the .desktop suffix. Missing entries are filtered at
# apply time, so it is safe to list a tool that only some builds install.
#
# GUI pentest tools only. Anything CLI-first (nxc, ffuf, the pipx venvs) has no
# .desktop file at all and belongs in a terminal, not the app grid.

# Burp and Ghidra ship no usable entry of their own — module 07 generates a
# stable one for each (install4j randomises its id; Ghidra only gets a PATH shim
# from module 50, so it never reached the app grid at all).
w1ld0s-burpsuite.desktop
w1ld0s-ghidra.desktop
dk.gqrx.gqrx.desktop          # SDR, from module 70
org.remmina.Remmina.desktop   # RDP/VNC to targets
# Not listed: wireshark and zaproxy. Nothing in tools.d installs them, so an
# entry here would be permanently filtered out — add the package first.
